  "slug": "metabolic-trait-robustness-microbial-e869",
  "summary": "Three database updates expand curated, quantitative enzyme and regulatory data with programmatic access, supporting enzyme and metabolic engineering workflows.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is curated, quantitative data resources for enzyme function and metabolic engineering. OrganiZymeDB compiles 28,121 manually curated stability and function measurements in organic solvents from 646 publications. SABIO-RK has been redesigned around a unified JSON curation framework, with a 60+ field search, saved results and a RESTful API returning JSON, CSV, SBML or EnzymeML. YEASTRACT+ adds quantitative TF-target regulation data for 13 yeasts, with tools for ranking TFs in transcriptomics data and TF-informed metabolic engineering. What is new is the emphasis on structured, quantitative records and standardized export formats rather than qualitative annotation. The items are heterogeneous: two address enzyme biochemistry and one addresses transcriptional regulation, so the shared thread is data infrastructure, not a demonstrated field-wide trend.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-10"
}
